Frame interpolation while the camera turns (issue #8).

A turn moves Baroque's view about one wall-tile width per game frame, so
the nearest identical tile is the neighbour (the room seemed not to move),
new faces entering at the screen edge had no history, and corners rounded
a pixel apart froze the room in geometry_weld. Under a detected camera
shift (voted from every face) the matcher predicts positions, follows shared
edges between faces, gives entering faces a history from their neighbours,
and lets corners within a pixel share one motion. Every face still has to
pass geometry_pair_valid and the weld. Without a detected shift (standing
still, walking forward) matching is unchanged.

tests/geometry_interp.c: camera_turn test; the reference comparison skips
scenes that are detected as turns.

